        description
            Build Compiled and the compiler from @spec.Compile and @spec.Diagnostics, with compound states, history, 
            `Flow.input`, private and computed fields and the snapshot shape (slice 3a).

            **Why now:** the skeleton compiles only the Pay machine; the full construction rules and the diagnostics 
            are unbuilt, and every module after this reads Compiled.

            **Read first:** @spec.Compile, @spec.Diagnostics, @task.V3.T13 (the static cases that judge it), 
            code:packages/flow-state-v3/conformance/README.md (the round-14 carry list).

            **Split (orchestrator, 2026-11-12, wide consult W3, item 3):** fragments, `.each`, subject paths (replacing 
            `owner` and `current`) and multi-step schedules moved to @task.V3.T57, which waits for the wide consult's 
            question 11 rulings. Codes split as proposed below; the lead may move a code between the two with a note. 
            Read code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/fable-wide-consult-2026-11-12.md (W3).

            **Scope added** (the user, 2026-11-11, from 
            code:workflow/plans/flow/references/proposals/plan-task-coverage-2026-11-11.md): name the author-facing 
            features, each passing a case on production: Flow.input, computed Flow.initial, Flow.private, one source 
            per field, ImpureDefault, creation purity, identity inputs, compound states and Flow.state traits, context 
            slots, the Definition Schemas, E.X with InvalidEvent, payload checks and app entries (rows M03 to M16, M19 
            to M21, M35 to M37, M39 to M41, R01 to R03; @plan.Machines.O1, @plan.Runtime.O1). Also own handler(), 
            guard(), Flow.state and the "Flow outermost" type rule (M05, M13, M22), which no Spec states, and 
            Invariants for Compile R10, R13 and R14 (a Spec revision). **Owed checks** (no Invariant or case today): 
            M06, M19, M39, M40, M41 (Compile R14), M23, M24, M27, M28 (Compile R10) and M33 (Compile R11). Fragment 
            inputs go to T57.

            **Read first (added):** @plan.Machines.O1, @plan.Runtime.O1, @plan.Diagnostics.O1.

            **Slice 3a, machine structure (replan, accepted 2026-11-11; split 2026-11-12):** the compiler and turn for 
            compound states, history and subroutines, raise and notify, `Flow.input` (compile half; the naming half is 
